// Bug 239 (FIXED), Codex review r9: `defs`'s newtype `read` has a method `owned`, called from
// `main` as `r.owned()`. Its Core spelling `read_owned` is also a compiler intrinsic's, and Lower
// recognised an intrinsic for any call spelling no function of the module being lowered defines,
// so the method call became the intrinsic (a load through `&r`: 7) while `--interp` ran the method
// (42). A method call names a program method; intrinsics are free calls.
// Expected: 42, natively and --interp.
mod defs {
    pub newtype read = Int;
    impl read {
        pub fn owned(&self) -> Int { return 42; }
    }
    pub fn seven() -> read { return read(7); }
}
import defs.{read, seven};
fn main() -> Int {
    let r: read = seven();
    return r.owned();
}
